<title>INDIA: India 97/98 divestment target 48 bln rupees.</title>
<headline>India 97/98 divestment target 48 bln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>India expects to take in 48 billion rupees from the sale of government stakes in state-controlled firms in 1997/98 (April-March), Finance Minister P. Chidambaram said on Friday.  </p>
<p>Chidambaram said the government planned to sell its stakes in three state-controlled firms -- Gas Authority of India Ltd, Modern Food Industries (India) Ltd and the India Tourism Development Corp -- as suggested by the Disinvestment Commission.</p>
